efore {\n      content: \"○\";\n      position: absolute;\n      top: 0;\n      left: 0;\n      color: #2699c9;\n      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 12px;\n      line-height: 22px;\n    }\n\n    .red {\n      color: #e31b23;\n    }\n\n    .blue {\n      color: #168bc2;\n      font-family: \"SimSun\", \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n    }\n\n    .nowrap {\n      white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n\n    .intro .points {\n      margin-bottom: 1px;\n    }\n\n    .pros .points {\n      margin-bottom: 1px;\n    }\n\n    .cons .points {\n      margin-bottom: 1px;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"page\">\n    <div class=\"title\">如何看待线上教育?</div>\n\n    <section class=\"section intro\">\n      <div class=\"section-heading\">Introduction<span class=\"cn\">开头</span></div>\n      <ul class=\"points\">\n        <li class=\"point\">\n          <span class=\"red\">The pandemic is ranging across the globe, and students are reeling from it.</span><br>\n          <span class=\"blue\">（背景）</span> During the lockdown, students have no other choice but to study<br>\n          from home, making online education more popular.　<span class=\"blue\">（引出话题）</span>\n          <span class=\"red\">In my<br>\n          view, it has both pros and cons, and should be used wisely.</span> <span class=\"blue\">（抛出观点）</span>\n        </li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"section pros\">\n      <div class=\"section-heading\">Pros<span class=\"cn\">好处</span></div>\n      <ul class=\"points\">\n        <li class=\"point\">\n          For students, online education is more flexible. <span class=\"red\">Rather than being<br>\n          restricted in classrooms,</span> leaners can sign up for any course they are<br>\n          interested in as long as they have the access to the Internet.　<span class=\"blue\">（对于学生，<br>\n          课程选择更加灵活）</span>\n        </li>\n        <li class=\"point\">\n          For teachers, they don’t need to make the <span class=\"red\">roll call,</span> because the system can<br>\n          record automatically. Besides, they can also assign, collect and review the<br>\n          homework more conveniently.　<span class=\"blue\">（对于老师，教学更加便捷）</span>\n        </li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"section cons\">\n      <div class=\"section-heading\">Cons<span class=\"cn\">不足</span></div>\n      <ul class=\"points\">\n        <li class=\"point\">\n          Online courses may be effective for <span class=\"red\">self-directed</span> learners, but students<br>\n          who are not organized and in possession of good time-management skills<br>\n          may struggle.　<span class=\"blue\">（对于自驱型学习者有效，反之，效果不佳）</span>\n        </li>\n        <li class=\"point\">\n          Online education is lacking in teacher-student interaction. It’s more<br>\n          difficult for teachers to ask feedbacks from students. And students also<br>\n          can’t ask questions immediately.　<span class=\"blue\">（师生间缺少互动）</span>\n        </li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"section conclusion\">\n      <div class=\"section-heading\">Conclusion<span class=\"cn\">结论</span></div>\n      <ul class=\"points\">\n        <li class=\"point\">\n          Therefore, students should ask themselves whether they are capable of<br>\n          learning independently before signing up for online coursework.　<span class=\"blue\">（所以在<br>\n          参与线上课程之前，学生首先应该对自己的自主学习能力有所判断）</span>\n        </li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>"
